<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE niftoolsxml>
<niftoolsxml version="0.10.0.0">

    <!--
    NIF-CS.xml: Community Shaders (https://github.com/community-shaders/skyrim-community-shaders)
    additions to nif.xml. NifSkope loads this file after nif.xml from the same folder, so that
    nif.xml itself stays unchanged.

    SPECS
    All Community Shaders changes live in <spec> elements. Only one spec is applied at a time:
    the one selected in File > Community Shaders PBR Spec, or the spec with default="true".
    Selecting another spec reloads the XML and the current NIF. When Community Shaders changes
    its PBR NIF format, add a new <spec version="2" ...> beside version 1, and move
    default="true" to it once it is released. Keep version 1 so that older NIFs can still be
    inspected.

    PATCHES
    Besides declaring new types as in nif.xml, a spec can patch existing declarations with
    patch="true":
    - enum / bitflags: each option adds or replaces the option with the same value.
    - niobject / struct: each field is one of these operations, applied in order:
      - rename="New Name" [hide="true"] cond="..." [vercond="..."]
        Display-only: show the existing field as "New Name" while the conditions hold. The field
        keeps its name, type and value, so code reading it is unaffected. The element text
        replaces the description. For several renames of a field, the first match is shown.
        With hide="true" (rename is then optional), the field is also hidden in the tree view
        while the conditions hold, but still read and written. Hidden fields are shown again
        when NifSkope is set to show non-applicable rows.
      - value="N" rename="New Name" cond="..." [vercond="..."]
        Display-only: show the enum option N of the existing field as "New Name" while the
        conditions hold, in the value and in the editor. The stored value is unchanged.
      - andcond="..." [vercond="..."]
        The existing field is only read/written if this condition also holds. With vercond, the
        restriction only applies to the versions matching vercond.
      - after="Existing Field" plus the usual field attributes [hide="true"]
        Insert a new field after the last field named "Existing Field" (and after the fields
        inserted there before). With hide="true", the new field is always hidden.
    Tokens declared inside a spec are replaced before the nif.xml tokens, so they can use them.
    -->


    <!--
    Community Shaders TruePBR, NIF format v1.

    Source: src/TruePBR.cpp (BSLightingShaderProperty_LoadBinary, _PostLinkObject) and
    src/TruePBR/BSLightingShaderMaterialPBR.cpp (LoadBinary) of Community Shaders.

    PBR is enabled on a BSLightingShaderProperty (Skyrim / SSE) by Shader Flags 2 bit 23
    (SLSF2 "Unused01", kMenuScreen in CommonLibSSE). The material is then read as for shader type
    Default, so only shader types Default (0) and MultiLayer Parallax (11) are meaningful:
    - The base material fields keep their place, with a PBR meaning (renamed below).
    - Shader type MultiLayer Parallax: its 5 floats hold the coat, fuzz or glint parameters.
    - Other shader types: Community Shaders does not read their own parameters.
    With PBR, shader types Default and MultiLayer Parallax and the Shader Flags 2 bits are shown
    under their PBR names, and fields that the active features do not use are hidden.

    Features, selected by other Shader Flags 2 bits (CS decides in this order):
    - Multi_Layer_Parallax (24): Two Layer (clear coat). Then also:
        Soft_Lighting (25) Interlayer Parallax, Back_Lighting (27) Coat Normal,
        Effect_Lighting (30) Colored Coat.
    - else Back_Lighting (27): Hair Marschner, with no other features.
    - else:
        Anisotropic_Lighting (21) Thin Surface, Effect_Lighting (30) Foliage,
        Rim_Lighting (26) Subsurface,
        Soft_Lighting (25) Fuzz, or else Fit_Slope (12) Glint.

    Textures (BSShaderTextureSet): 0 base color, 1 normal, 2 emissive, 3 displacement
    (fuzz roughness in green, see PBRFuzz), 5 RMAOS (roughness, metallic, AO, specular level),
    6 fuzz (color, weight) or coat normal (normal, roughness), 7 subsurface (color, thickness)
    or coat (color, strength).

    Extra data on the shader property, ignored with Two Layer and Hair Marschner (these cannot
    be named here, since conditions cannot test the extra data name):
    - NiFloatsExtraData "PBRThinSurface", 4 floats: subsurface balance (0-1, default 0.75),
      thin surface front specular weight (0-1, default 0.5), back specular weight (0-1,
      default 0.5), back roughness scale (0-3, default 1).
    - NiFloatsExtraData "PBRFuzz", 2 floats: fuzz roughness (0-1, negative uses the base
      roughness), use the displacement texture green channel as fuzz roughness (0 or 1).
    -->
    <spec version="1" name="v1: TruePBR, Shader Flags 2 bit 23" default="true">

        <token name="cspbr1" attrs="cond">
            Community Shaders PBR v1 features, from Shader Flags 2.
            NOTE: Composite tokens first, so that the tokens they use are replaced after them.
            NOTE: NifExpr applies ! to everything after it, so negated terms must be in parentheses.
            <cspbr1 token="#CS1_NO_LAYER_PARAMS#" string="(#CS1_PBR# #AND# (!#CS1_TWO_LAYER#) #AND# (!#CS1_FUZZ#) #AND# (!#CS1_GLINT#))">PBR without Two Layer, Fuzz or Glint.</cspbr1>
            <cspbr1 token="#CS1_PBR#" string="((Shader Flags 2 #BITAND# 0x800000) != 0)">PBR.</cspbr1>
            <cspbr1 token="#CS1_NOT_PBR#" string="((Shader Flags 2 #BITAND# 0x800000) == 0)">Not PBR.</cspbr1>
            <cspbr1 token="#CS1_TWO_LAYER#" string="((Shader Flags 2 #BITAND# 0x1800000) == 0x1800000)">PBR, Multi_Layer_Parallax.</cspbr1>
            <cspbr1 token="#CS1_SUBSURFACE#" string="((Shader Flags 2 #BITAND# 0xD800000) == 0x4800000)">PBR, Rim_Lighting, not Multi_Layer_Parallax or Back_Lighting.</cspbr1>
            <cspbr1 token="#CS1_FUZZ#" string="((Shader Flags 2 #BITAND# 0xB800000) == 0x2800000)">PBR, Soft_Lighting, not Multi_Layer_Parallax or Back_Lighting.</cspbr1>
            <cspbr1 token="#CS1_GLINT#" string="((Shader Flags 2 #BITAND# 0xB801000) == 0x801000)">PBR, Fit_Slope, not Multi_Layer_Parallax, Back_Lighting or Soft_Lighting.</cspbr1>
        </token>

        <!-- Unused01 keeps its name; once set, the Shader Flags 2 bits show their PBR names (below) -->
        <bitflags name="SkyrimShaderPropertyFlags2" patch="true">
            <option bit="23" name="Unused01">Unused? Community Shaders: enables TruePBR (kMenuScreen). The material fields and flags are then shown under their PBR names. Textures: 0 base color, 1 normal, 2 emissive, 3 displacement, 5 RMAOS, 6 fuzz or coat normal, 7 subsurface or coat.</option>
        </bitflags>

        <!-- Shader Type (declared in NiObjectNET for BSLightingShaderProperty): PBR names of the
             two shader types that PBR uses; the others keep their names -->
        <niobject name="NiObjectNET" patch="true">
            <field name="Shader Type" value="0" rename="PBR" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR material, the features are selected by Shader Flags 2. Coat, fuzz and glint parameters are the defaults: use PBR Two Layer/Fuzz/Glint to set them (the default fuzz weight is 0).</field>
            <field name="Shader Type" value="11" rename="PBR Two Layer/Fuzz/Glint" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR material with the coat (Two_Layer), fuzz (Fuzz) or glint (Glint) parameters, depending on Shader Flags 2.</field>
        </niobject>

        <niobject name="BSLightingShaderProperty" patch="true">
            <!-- Shader Flags 2 bits: PBR names, in the order Community Shaders decides the features -->
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="23" rename="PBR" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Community Shaders TruePBR.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="24" rename="Two_Layer" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Two Layer (clear coat) model.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="25" rename="Interlayer_Parallax" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_TWO_LAYER#">Two Layer: parallax between the layers.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="25" rename="Fuzz" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Fuzz (sheen), without Two_Layer and Hair_Marschner.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="27" rename="Coat_Normal" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_TWO_LAYER#">Two Layer: coat normal map (texture 6).</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="27" rename="Hair_Marschner" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Marschner hair shading, without Two_Layer. Disables the other features.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="30" rename="Colored_Coat" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_TWO_LAYER#">Two Layer: the coat color tints the diffuse lighting.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="30" rename="Foliage" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Foliage, without Two_Layer and Hair_Marschner.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="26" rename="Subsurface" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Subsurface scattering, without Two_Layer and Hair_Marschner.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="21" rename="Thin_Surface" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Thin Surface (light transmission through thin geometry), without Two_Layer and Hair_Marschner. Parameters from a "PBRThinSurface" NiFloatsExtraData.</field>
            <field name="Shader Flags 2" value="12" rename="Glint" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">Glint, without Two_Layer, Hair_Marschner and Fuzz. The parameters are read with shader type MultiLayer Parallax, otherwise defaults are used.</field>

            <!-- Base material fields used as in vanilla, except as described -->
            <field name="Emissive Color" rename="Emissive Color" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: multiplies the emissive texture (2), with Own_Emit. No effect without an emissive texture.</field>
            <field name="Emissive Multiple" rename="Emissive Multiple" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: multiplies the emissive texture (2). No effect without an emissive texture.</field>

            <!-- Base material fields: same place, PBR meaning -->
            <field name="Glossiness" rename="Specular Level" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: specular reflectance (F0) of non-metals, multiplied by the RMAOS alpha. Usually 0.04.</field>

            <field name="Specular Color" rename="Coat Color" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_TWO_LAYER#">PBR Two Layer: coat color, multiplied by the coat texture (7) color.</field>
            <field name="Specular Color" rename="Subsurface Color" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_SUBSURFACE#">PBR Subsurface: subsurface color, multiplied by the subsurface texture (7) color.</field>
            <field name="Specular Color" rename="Unused Color" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: unused. Subsurface Color with Rim_Lighting, Coat Color with Multi_Layer_Parallax (not with Back_Lighting alone).</field>

            <field name="Specular Strength" rename="Roughness Scale" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: multiplies the RMAOS roughness.</field>

            <field name="Lighting Effect 1" rename="Coat Strength" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_TWO_LAYER#">PBR Two Layer: coat strength, multiplied by the coat texture (7) alpha.</field>
            <field name="Lighting Effect 1" rename="Subsurface Opacity" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_SUBSURFACE#">PBR Subsurface: subsurface opacity (thickness), multiplied by the subsurface texture (7) alpha.</field>
            <field name="Lighting Effect 1" rename="Unused" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: unused. Subsurface Opacity with Rim_Lighting, Coat Strength with Multi_Layer_Parallax (not with Back_Lighting alone).</field>

            <field name="Lighting Effect 2" rename="Displacement Scale" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: height scale of the displacement texture (3).</field>

            <!-- MultiLayer Parallax parameters: PBR reads the same 5 floats with another layout -->
            <field name="Parallax Inner Layer Thickness" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" andcond="#CS1_NOT_PBR#" />
            <field name="Parallax Refraction Scale" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" andcond="#CS1_NOT_PBR#" />
            <field name="Parallax Inner Layer Texture Scale" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" andcond="#CS1_NOT_PBR#" />
            <field name="Parallax Envmap Strength" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" andcond="#CS1_NOT_PBR#" />

            <field name="Coat Roughness" type="float" default="1.0" range="#F0_1#" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_TWO_LAYER#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Two Layer: coat roughness, multiplied by the coat normal texture (6) alpha.</field>
            <field name="Coat Specular Level" type="float" default="0.04" range="#F0_1#" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_TWO_LAYER#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Two Layer: specular reflectance (F0) of the coat.</field>
            <field name="Unused" type="float" length="3" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_TWO_LAYER#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Two Layer: unused.</field>

            <field name="Fuzz Color" type="Color3" default="#VEC3_ONE#" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_FUZZ#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Fuzz: fuzz color, multiplied by the fuzz texture (6) color.</field>
            <field name="Fuzz Weight" type="float" default="1.0" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_FUZZ#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Fuzz: fuzz weight, multiplied by the fuzz texture (6) alpha.</field>
            <field name="Fuzz Roughness" type="float" default="1.0" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_FUZZ#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Fuzz: fuzz roughness if below 1, otherwise the base roughness is used. A "PBRFuzz" NiFloatsExtraData overrides it.</field>

            <field name="Glint Screen Space Scale" type="float" default="1.5" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_GLINT#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Glint: screen space scale.</field>
            <field name="Glint Log Microfacet Density" type="float" default="40.0" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_GLINT#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Glint: log microfacet density.</field>
            <field name="Glint Microfacet Roughness" type="float" default="0.015" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_GLINT#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Glint: microfacet roughness.</field>
            <field name="Glint Density Randomization" type="float" default="2.0" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_GLINT#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Glint: density randomization.</field>
            <field name="Unused" type="float" default="1.0" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_GLINT#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR Glint: unused (fuzz roughness with Fuzz).</field>

            <field name="Unused" type="float" length="5" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="(Shader Type == 11) #AND# #CS1_NO_LAYER_PARAMS#" after="Parallax Envmap Strength">PBR without Two Layer, Fuzz or Glint: unused. Coat parameters with Multi_Layer_Parallax, fuzz parameters with Soft_Lighting, glint parameters with Fit_Slope.</field>

            <!-- Parameters of the other shader types: not read by Community Shaders with PBR -->
            <field name="Environment Map Scale" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Environment Map shader type.</field>
            <field name="Skin Tint Color" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Skin Tint shader type.</field>
            <field name="Hair Tint Color" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Hair Tint shader type.</field>
            <field name="Max Passes" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Parallax Occ shader type.</field>
            <field name="Scale" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Parallax Occ shader type.</field>
            <field name="Sparkle Parameters" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Sparkle Snow shader type.</field>
            <field name="Eye Cubemap Scale" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Eye Envmap shader type.</field>
            <field name="Left Eye Reflection Center" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Eye Envmap shader type.</field>
            <field name="Right Eye Reflection Center" hide="true" vercond="#BS_SKY_SSE#" cond="#CS1_PBR#">PBR: not read by Community Shaders, which ignores the Eye Envmap shader type.</field>
        </niobject>

    </spec>

</niftoolsxml>
